I had a really good human tourist going. Had just returned from after
purchasing 1900z worth of protection at XPlvl1 rates (about 6 points).
I also had a few nice +1 pieces of armour too. Total AC was about -6,
more than enough to deal with the monsters I was encountering at this
depth. Skilled in short sword, and all set to go up to expert and start
twoweaponing. (Something I realy want to experiment with.)

I was holding an uncursed magic lamp, had price-IDed two ID scrolls,
had wands of teleport, invis *and* cancellation (along with some unIDed
ones) and had a good old pile of handy stuff sitting by the stairs
while I went to find a box or chest to put it all in.

Just into the next room, dealing with a particularly foul-mouthed
dretch, when I saw that about a dozen mordor orcs had just spawned
right on top of my stash. I see them picking up armour and weapons, and
I immediately realise that there is a wand of invisible there as well
as a load of unIDed scrolls and potions. I turn round and run back,
blasting the orcs generously with a wand of lightning and leaving my
dogs to deal with the dretch. One of the orcs zaps himself invisible.
No problem, I'll still find him and kill him. "You hear a chugging
sound --more--   It rips out of its armour!" Great, one of those
potions was polymorph and now I have an unknown invisible monster to
deal with. Killed the rest of the orcs easily, but that last one came
up to me and started swinging. I wasn't hitting it with my sword, so I
tried the old camera trick. No joy- obviosuly the light from the camera
flash passes right through the retinas of invisible monsters. So I
fired off a few rounds of lightning as well- they all missed, and I was
killed.

No bones, natch.

Moral of the story? Always use a box or chest. Drag it down from Dlvl1
if need be. 
*sigh*



